<%# ICODOS override of notifications_settings/_reminder_banner.html.erb
    Upstream renders the "unlock with DocuSeal Pro" upsell, which does not apply
    here.

    RENDERS NOTHING WHEN ALL IS WELL. Counts, "last checked" and other status
    were removed on request: they are noise on a settings page, and the numbers
    change on their own so they read as clutter rather than information.

    What remains are the two states a person must not miss, because in both of
    them reminders are NOT reaching anyone:
      - test mode, where the schedule is worked out but no email is sent
      - a stalled scheduler, which is the exact failure this feature exists to
        prevent (something that looks switched on and quietly stopped)

    ONLY USE TAILWIND/DAISYUI CLASSES DOCUSEAL ALREADY USES SOMEWHERE. The CSS in
    /app/public/packs is precompiled and Tailwind purged the rest, so an unused
    class silently does nothing — no error, just wrong layout. gap-x-6, gap-x-3,
    alert-error, alert-warning, md:join-horizontal and leading-snug are absent.
    Verify before using:
      grep -F 'the-class' /app/public/packs/css/application-*.css

    CHECK ON EVERY DOCUSEAL VERSION BUMP — a stale override renders silently.
%>
<% status = IcodosReminderSweep.status(current_account) rescue { error: 'unavailable' } %>

<% if status[:error] %>
  <p class="mt-2 mb-2 text-sm text-red-400 font-bold">
    Reminder status is unavailable: <%= status[:error] %>
  </p>
<% elsif status[:enabled] && status[:dry_run] %>
  <p class="mt-2 mb-2 text-sm text-red-400 font-bold">
    Test mode: reminders are worked out but no email is actually sent.
  </p>
<% elsif status[:enabled] && status[:stale] %>
  <p class="mt-2 mb-2 text-sm text-red-400 font-bold">
    Nothing has been checked for over two hours, so reminders are not going out.
    The scheduled task on the server has probably stopped.
  </p>
<% elsif !status[:enabled] %>
  <p class="mt-2 mb-2 text-sm text-red-400 font-bold">
    Reminders are switched off on the server, so nobody is being chased.
  </p>
<% end %>
